When the owner is a module, the function checks whether the module defines a `__getattr__` attribute. If `owner.getattr("__getattr__")` succeeds, the function immediately returns `False`, meaning no-member is **not** emitted — this lets modules with dynamic attribute handlers (a module-level `__getattr__`) skip the member check. If `astroid.NotFoundError` is raised (no `__getattr__` defined), the check continues normally.
